<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1964–2017</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FARC, FARC-EP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (FARC) was a Marxist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> group founded in 1964 by Manuel Marulanda and others from peasant self-defence groups. Increasingly financed by kidnapping and the drug trade, it fought the Colombian state for more than five decades. After a peace agreement signed in 2016 with President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-santos">Juan Manuel Santos</a> it disarmed and became a political party, though dissident groups fought on.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolutionary-armed-forces-of-colombia.jpg" alt="Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MrPenguin20 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_FARC-EP.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
